<title>FRANCE: Saudis buy barley subject confirmation - trade.</title>
<headline>Saudis buy barley subject confirmation - trade.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia appears to have lined up purchasess of 500,000 tonnes of optional-origin barley at around $152 per tonne and above, but the deal is subject to final confirmation from Riyadh, which is expected later on Wednesday, grain traders said.</p>
<p>The barley is for delivery in late April and May.  </p>
<p>Prices include cost and freight.</p>
<p>&quot;They have bought but we are waiting for confirmation,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia tendered on Tuesday for 500,000 tonnes of barley with the following delivery timetable.</p>
<p>    2nd half April		 50,000	Dammam</p>
<p>    2nd half April		 50,000	Jeddah</p>
<p>    1st half May		   50,000	Dammam</p>
<p>    1st half May		  100,000	Jeddah</p>
<p>    2nd half May		  100,000	Dammam</p>
<p>    2nd half May		  150,000	Jeddah</p>
</text>
